Let the given matrix be $A = \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix}$.
We want to find the determinant of $A$. We can calculate the determinant as follows:
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \csc^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x) + \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x - 1) \\ &= \cot^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= (\cot^2 x - \cos^2 x) \sin^2 x \\ &= \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \cos^2 x \right) \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x \left( \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} - 1 \right) \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x \left( \frac{1 - \sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \right) \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x (1 - \sin^2 x) \\ &= \cos^2 x \cos^2 x \\ &= \cos^4 x \end{align*}
The determinant is $\cos^4 x$.

\boxed{\cos^4 x}

\boxed{\cos^4 x}

