We are given that $|z|=5$, and we want to find $|\overline{z}^2|$.

First, we know that the magnitude of a complex number is non-negative. Additionally, for any complex number $z$, we have $|z| = |\overline{z}|$. Therefore, $|\overline{z}^2| = | \overline{z} |^2$.
Since $|z| = 5$, we have $|\overline{z}| = |z| = 5$.
So, $|\overline{z}^2| = |\overline{z}|^2 = 5^2 = 25$.

\boxed{25} 

