Let $V_1$ be the volume of the original cube. The side length of the original cube is 2 cm. Thus, $V_1 = 2^3 = 8$ cubic centimeters.
The volume of the new cube is $V_2 = V_1 + 19 = 8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters.
Let $s$ be the side length of the new cube. Then $s^3 = V_2 = 27$. Taking the cube root of both sides gives $s = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$ cm.

